549
00:22:18,435 --> 00:22:20,113
then, is philosophy.

550
00:22:20,293 --> 00:22:23,049
The F50 was a supercar you operated

551
00:22:23,049 --> 00:22:25,963
with a manual lever and no electronic

552
00:22:25,963 --> 00:22:26,829
safety net.

553
00:22:27,009 --> 00:22:29,814
The Enzo replaced it with automation,

554
00:22:29,814 --> 00:22:32,164
ceramic brakes and active aero.

555
00:22:32,344 --> 00:22:34,337
That's our reading of the sources,

556
00:22:34,337 --> 00:22:36,036
not a statement from Ferrari.

557
00:22:36,216 --> 00:22:38,601
Each choice made the car faster in

558
00:22:38,601 --> 00:22:41,197
one way and less engaging in another.

559
00:22:41,547 --> 00:22:43,627
What we could not confirm:

560
00:22:43,627 --> 00:22:46,027
the F50's real original price,

561
00:22:46,027 --> 00:22:48,187
with figures of four fifty,

562
00:22:48,187 --> 00:22:52,507
four eighty-seven and three hundred forty-two thousand

563
00:22:52,507 --> 00:22:56,267
pounds; the Enzo's true production total; which

564
00:22:56,267 --> 00:22:59,227
Formula One engine the F50 came from;

565
00:22:59,227 --> 00:23:02,748
the Enzo's Fiorano time; the Enzo's steering

566
00:23:02,748 --> 00:23:07,228
assistance; and a like-for-like running-cost comparison.

567
00:23:07,408 --> 00:23:09,289
We flagged each as it came up.

568
00:23:09,639 --> 00:23:11,504
That is the difference between the Ferrari

569
00:23:11,504 --> 00:23:12,659
Enzo and the F50 as far as

570
00:23:12,659 --> 00:23:13,458
the evidence goes.

571
00:23:13,638 --> 00:23:14,707
One is quicker,

572
00:23:14,707 --> 00:23:16,773
and the other more involving.

